# AI Council orchestration

Read **`docs/council/COUNCIL_SYSTEM.md`** for personalities and output format. **Setup:** `docs/council/CHAIR_SETUP.md` (pinned Chair chat — no copy/paste).

Members: **Nala** (contrarian, highest authority), **London** (first principles), **Fasa** (expansionist). Lenses: `identities/_shared-smite-lens.md` + `identities/_shared-stress-test.md` (challenge before affirm; no glazing — same as `.cursor/rules/stress-test.mdc`).

## Triggers (run council flow when you see)

| Pattern | Action |
|---------|--------|
| **`go`** or **`>>go`** | **Always read** `docs/council/ui/pending-convene.json` first. If `status` is `"new"` and (`topic` or `attachments[]`), run **`npm run council:go`** (prepare + sequential plan), then execute the flow below **one member at a time**. When done: **`npm run council:status -- pending`**. If idle, tell user to Send in the panel first. **Images:** `attachments` lists saved files under `docs/council/ui/attachments/` — members must **Read** those paths (also in `council:prompt` output). |
| `>> <topic>` | `npm run council:prepare -- "<topic>"` then same sequential flow |
| `?nala <question>` / `?london` / `?fasa` | Solo member |
| **Convene council on:** … | Full council |
| **council:** … or **c:** … | Full council |

**Panel workflow:** user sends topic (and optional images — 📎, paste, or drag on the panel) in `npm run council:ui` → pending file → panel **auto-wakes** Cursor with `@council.mdc go` (or user types **`go`** manually) → you run council **sequentially** → transcript streams **live** on panel (`drafts/` + `live-status.json` + `sessions/latest.json`).

**Images in Chair chat (fallback):** If panel attach fails, user can **paste or attach images in this pinned Chair chat** and say **`go`** — **Read** those images (or paths they give) before convening members; include paths in member prompts when you run `council:prompt`.

## Config

- `docs/council/council.config.json` — `nala`, `london`, `fasa`
- Models: `auto`, `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking`, `claude-opus-4-8-thinking-high`, `composer-2.5-fast`, `gpt-5.3-codex`, `gpt-5.5-medium`

## Natural language model changes

**Nala switch to Claude**, **Fasa use GPT**, etc. → `npm run council:config -- <id> model <slug>`, confirm, then solo if they asked to answer.

## Full council session (LIVE panel — user watches http://localhost:3939)

**Sequential only** — same feel as `npm run council:chat-demo`. Never launch all three Tasks in parallel.

1. **`npm run council:go`** (panel topic) or **`npm run council:prepare -- "<topic>"`** (`>>` path)
2. **Round 1** — for each member **nala → london → fasa**:
   - `npm run council:turn -- <id> 1` — panel shows only that member **thinking**
   - Launch **one** Task subagent for `<id>` only (`npm run council:prompt -- <id>` for context)
   - While composing (optional): `npm run council:draft -- <id> 1 "text so far"` after each sentence
   - **`npm run council:append -- <sessionId> <id> 1 "…"`** — **await** (char-by-char stream + read pause). Do **not** start the next member until append finishes.
3. **Round 2 pause** — `npm run council:status -- reset --round=2` (auto pause so user reads R1)
4. **Round 2** — same order **nala → london → fasa**:
   - `npm run council:turn -- <id> 2`
   - One Task per member; Round 2 must **@mention** peers and respond to their R1/R2 lines
   - `npm run council:append -- <sessionId> <id> 2 "…"` — await each
5. `npm run council:status -- chair running "Synthesizing Final Verdict…"`
6. `npm run council:decide -- "…"` (max 45 words) — **auto-extracts tasks** into `TASKS.md` when the verdict or transcript mentions actionable items (see below)
7. `npm run council:status -- pending` — marks panel queue done
8. Post format from COUNCIL_SYSTEM.md

**Auto task extract (on `decide`):** Parses Final Verdict + Round 1/2 transcript for imperatives (`ship`, `pick`, `rank`, …), `GOALS items — A, B, C`, and explicit `TASK: Title` markers. Writes new rows to **TASKS.md**, **mod log** (one bubble per task + summary), **`npm run vault:sync`**. Skips duplicates already in Pending. Disable once: `npm run council:decide -- --no-extract "verdict only"`.

**Chair tip:** For precise tasks, include in the verdict: `TASK: Conquest Map MVP; TASK: Currency system polish`

**Critical:** **`council:append` uses the same live typing as chat-demo** (draft files + char stream). **Never** `--instant` during live convenes. **Never** batch three appends back-to-back.

**Pacing (config):** `typeMsPerChar` ~12ms, **2.2s pause** after each reply, **4.5s** before Round 2. Tune in `docs/council/council.config.json`.

## Repo writes (Chair / agents — edit access)

When the user asks Council to **create tasks**, **log bugs**, or **apply the verdict** to project files:

| Command | Effect |
|---------|--------|
| `npm run council:write-task -- "Title" #builds #shop` | Appends **TASKS.md** § Pending, **mod log**, **`npm run vault:sync`** |
| `npm run council:write-bug -- "Title"` | Appends **BUGS.md** § Open, mod log, vault sync |
| `npm run council:mod-log` | Print recent mod-log entries |

**Auto extract:** `council:decide` runs task extraction by default (`autoExtractVerdictTasks` in config). Manual items still work:

| `npm run council:write-task -- "Title" #builds` | Force-add one task |
| `npm run council:write-bug -- "Title"` | Force-add one bug |

After **Final Verdict**, extracted tasks appear as **MOD LOG** bubbles in the panel (no extra Chair steps unless you used `--no-extract`).

**Bug reports from user** (any chat): follow **`.cursor/rules/bugs.mdc`** — `BUGS.md` + `vault:sync`.

**Vault:** Task/bug board mirrors update automatically when write commands run.

## Response style

Human group chat — **40–55 words R1**, **30–45 R2**, **one bubble per reply**. Plain English. Round 2 @mention at least one peer. **No praise openers** — stress-test the topic first (`_shared-stress-test.md`). Final Verdict names at least one risk.

**Status helpers:**
- `npm run council:turn -- nala 1` — one member thinking, others waiting/done
- `npm run council:status -- phase round2 "Reading Round 1…"`
- `npm run council:draft -- nala 1 "partial text so far"`

## Solo member

`?nala …` or **Nala answer …** → optional prepare, one Task with identity + model, reply in voice only.
